meta {
  name: Attach DataSinks to Pipeline
  type: http
  seq: 9
}

patch {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/datasets/:dataSetId/pipelines/:id
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

params:path {
  dataSetId: {{dataSetId}}
  id: {{pipelineId}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "dataSinkIds": ["{{pipelinesDataSinkId}}"]
  }
}

script:post-response {
  if (res.body && res.body.id) {
    bru.setVar('pipelineId', res.body.id);
  }
}

docs {
  **Precondition:** `dataSetId`, `pipelineId`, and `postgisDataSinkId` are set. Run after `pipelines/create-pipeline.bru` and `datasinks/create-postgis-datasink.bru`.

  **Expected Response:** 200 OK, body reflects the updated `dataSinkIds`. Other Pipeline fields remain unchanged.

  **Note:** This is an additive request — `pipelines/create-pipeline.bru`, `update-pipeline.bru`, and `patch-pipeline.bru` do not include `dataSinkIds` in their bodies, so they continue to work even when no DataSink has been created. Run this request only after you have a DataSink to attach.

  **System Impact:**

  | Layer | Effect |
  |---|---|
  | Backend | Pipeline-to-DataSink association recorded; the DataSink's `pipeline` reference is set by `PipelineService` |
  | Config Adapter | — (the association affects the saga trigger only when the parent DataSet is released) |
  | External System | — |
}
